- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/derivative.html
- Summary (EN): Measures how pixel values change along the horizontal and vertical axes of a layer, useful for tasks such as edge detection. Outputs dCdx and dCdy.
- Résumé (FR) : Calcule les dérivées horizontale et verticale d'une couche, utiles notamment pour détecter les contours.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the layer from which derivatives are computed"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Space: Image, Pixel or Local normalisation of the pixel size", "Angle: rotates the sampling positions; at 90 degrees the x derivative equals the y derivative at angle 0", "Scale: multiplies the output", "Offset: adds a value to the output", "Read Pixels outside Image: reads beyond the edge for Wrap textures, stays inside for Clamp edges", "Kernel Size: widens the distance between sampled pixels to smooth stepping", "Difference Mode: Central, Forward or Diagonal finite differences; Diagonal is described as smoothest"]

- Caveats: ["Boundary handling is a trade-off between wrapped and clamped textures.", "With slowly varying values and limited bit depth the default kernel may give stepped derivatives; raise Kernel Size."]

